---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import VideoSection from '../../components/VideoSection.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n/utils';

const lang: Lang = 'en';
---
<Base lang={lang} path="/events/undead/" title="Undead Siege: Complete Guide" description="Alliance defense against infected waves: the 300,000 clue bar, difficulty levels from 2.4M to 24.5M Enemy Might, the hidden multi-squad mechanic that kills 9.5M players, and full reward tables.">
  <GuidePage title="Undead Siege: Complete Guide" description="Alliance defense against infected waves: the 300,000 clue bar, difficulty levels from 2.4M to 24.5M Enemy Might, the hidden multi-squad mechanic that kills 9.5M players, and full reward tables." lang={lang}>
    <p>Undead Siege is the alliance defense event: your whole alliance stands against <strong>waves of infected</strong>, with heroes on the wall doing the fighting. Two rules define it before anything else: <strong>shields do not work</strong>, and it is <strong>not a points event</strong> — the goal is to defend as many waves as possible.</p>
    <p>This guide covers how sieges unlock, the difficulty ladder, the hidden multi-squad mechanic that wipes underprepared alliances, rewards, and the top seven mistakes.</p>

    <h2 id="unlocking">How a Siege Unlocks</h2>
    <p>Sieges are not on a timer — your alliance triggers them:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Fill the <strong>300,000 Clue Points</strong> bar.</li>
      <li>An <strong>R4 or R5 finds the hidden Death Prison</strong> on the map.</li>
      <li>That leader <strong>starts the siege and chooses the difficulty</strong>.</li>
      <li>The siege begins roughly <strong>4 hours after the click</strong> — use that gap to get every member&apos;s heroes on the wall.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Clue points come from normal daily play:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Attacking <strong>Rebels</strong> and the <strong>Blight Legion</strong></li>
      <li>Killing <strong>Wandering Blights</strong></li>
      <li>Gathering resources on tiles</li>
      <li>Helping allies (help-build and help-research taps)</li>
      <li>Running <strong>Alliance Excavation</strong></li>
      <li>Completing <strong>Falcon Quests</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>An active alliance fills the bar through ordinary play; the bar is not the bottleneck, readiness is.</p>

    <h2 id="difficulty">Difficulty Levels</h2>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Difficulty</th><th>Enemy Might</th><th>Territory</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Level 1</td><td>2.4M</td><td>Territory 13</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Level 6</td><td>~3 squads per wave</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Level 10</td><td>24.5M</td><td>Territory 27</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The ladder scales continuously from 2.4M Enemy Might at Level 1 up to 24.5M at Level 10, with territory requirements rising from 13 to 27. Higher difficulty levels also unlock <strong>Enemy Mutations</strong> — <strong>preview the mutations before committing</strong> to a difficulty, because a mutation that counters your defense comp is worth millions of Enemy Might.</p>

    <h2 id="hidden-mechanic">The Hidden Multi-Squad Mechanic</h2>
    <p>This is the part of the event the difficulty screen does not tell you, and it is the difference between surviving 20 waves and collapsing at 17:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The siege sends <strong>2 or more squads at the stated might</strong>. Stated 8M means you fight two squads of 8M — effectively double the number on the button.</li>
      <li>At <strong>wave 17</strong> of an 8M difficulty, the actual strength is roughly <strong>7.3M x 2</strong>.</li>
      <li>At <strong>difficulty 6 and above, waves send 3 squads</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>Squad HP persists between waves.</strong> Your tank starts the next fight at whatever HP it ended the last one — and your squad 1 must survive <strong>back-to-back fights</strong> with no heal in between.</li>
    </ul>
    <blockquote>A 9.5M player died at wave 17 of an 8M difficulty — worn down by consecutive fights with persistent HP. The stated might is not the fight.</blockquote>

    <h2 id="rewards">Rewards</h2>
    <h3 id="personal-rewards">Personal Milestones</h3>
    <p>Each player faces <strong>20 solo waves</strong>, with milestones at waves <strong>1, 4, 8, 10, 13, 16 and 20</strong> — tokens, upgrades and chests. If your city falls it will <strong>not be attacked again</strong>, but your personal rewards stop there: dying at wave 12 of 20 forfeits every milestone after it.</p>
    <h3 id="alliance-rewards">Alliance Milestones</h3>
    <table class="w-full mb-6 text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Alliance total waves</th><th>Rewards</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>50</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>100</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>150</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>200</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>250</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
        <tr><td>300</td><td>Hero XP, materials, medals</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Two rules around the alliance total:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Membership over 48 hours</strong> is required to receive alliance rewards — new joins don&apos;t collect.</li>
      <li><strong>Reinforcing other members doesn&apos;t double your personal rewards</strong> — it raises the alliance total. Do it anyway: the alliance milestones are the big payout.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The all-time record stands at <strong>1,193 waves</strong> in a single siege.</p>

    <h2 id="deployment">Deployment: Squads and Reinforcing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your strongest squad goes on your own wall.</strong> That squad carries your 20 personal waves.</li>
      <li><strong>The rest of your squads reinforce other members</strong> — reinforcing raises the alliance total, which is where the shared rewards live.</li>
      <li>Reinforcements land at the member&apos;s wall and fight the incoming waves with them — send them before the waves hit, not after the notification.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="top-mistakes">The Top 7 Mistakes</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Heroes not on the wall</strong> — the biggest killer. Heroes on the wall are the event; a wall with no heroes is a city waiting to fall.</li>
      <li><strong>Ignoring wall defense</strong> — there is <strong>no auto-defend</strong> in this event. Whatever you preset is what fights.</li>
      <li><strong>Starting without 100% clue completion</strong> — a rushed start wastes the 4-hour warning window.</li>
      <li><strong>Underestimating mutations</strong> — always read the mutation preview before choosing the difficulty.</li>
      <li><strong>Not reinforcing members</strong> — the alliance milestones need bodies on every wall, not just your own.</li>
      <li><strong>Starting with partial squads</strong> — a half-empty wall squad is a dead wall squad.</li>
      <li><strong>Logging off without preset defense</strong> — offline defense works, but <strong>only if it was pre-set</strong>. Set it, then sleep.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Run the event with those seven fixed and your alliance defends near its ceiling. Hero setup for the wall and squad composition are covered in the <a href="/heroes/">Heroes guide</a>.</p>

    <VideoSection topic="undead" lang={lang} />
  </GuidePage>
</Base>
